---------------------- YAW-FRICTION --------------------------------------------
0                      YawFrctMod  - Yaw-friction model {0: none, 1: friction independent of yaw-bearing force and bending moment, 2: friction with Coulomb terms depending on yaw-bearing force and bending moment, 3: user defined model} (switch)
300.0                  M_CSmax     - Maximum static Coulomb friction torque (N-m) [M_CSmax when YawFrctMod=1; |Fz|*M_CSmax when YawFrctMod=2 and Fz<0]
0.0                    M_FCSmax    - Maximum static Coulomb friction torque proportional to yaw bearing shear force (N-m) [sqrt(Fx^2+Fy^2)*M_FCSmax; only used when YawFrctMod=2]
0.0                    M_MCSmax    - Maximum static Coulomb friction torque proportional to yaw bearing bending moment (N-m) [sqrt(Mx^2+My^2)*M_MCSmax; only used when YawFrctMod=2]
40.0                   M_CD        - Dynamic Coulomb friction moment (N-m) [M_CD when YawFrctMod=1; |Fz|*M_CD when YawFrctMod=2 and Fz<0]
0.0                    M_FCD       - Dynamic Coulomb friction moment proportional to yaw bearing shear force (N-m) [sqrt(Fx^2+Fy^2)*M_FCD; only used when YawFrctMod=2]
0.0                    M_MCD       - Dynamic Coulomb friction moment proportional to yaw bearing bending moment (N-m) [sqrt(Mx^2+My^2)*M_MCD; only used when YawFrctMod=2]
0.0                    sig_v       - Linear viscous friction coefficient (N-m/(rad/s))
0.0                    sig_v2      - Quadratic viscous friction coefficient (N-m/(rad/s)^2)
0.0                    OmgCut      - Yaw angular velocity cutoff below which viscous friction is linearized (rad/s)
